# Regulatory and Legislative Assessment for Sustainable Finance Instruments in Seychelles

This plan executes the substantive work required by the SeyCCAT TOR — a full regulatory and legislative assessment. Legal qualifications are out of scope; the focus is on research, analysis, and recommendations.

## Approach: Three Phases → Four Tasks → Three Deliverables

The TOR defines **4 Tasks** (Scope of Work) and **3 Deliverables**. We execute them through **3 research phases** that the user specified, each producing files in numbered folders within `Task001/`.

```mermaid
graph TD
    P1["Phase 1: Map Existing Instruments"] --> T1["Task 1: Legal & Regulatory Framework"]
    P2["Phase 2: Research Seychelles Practice"] --> T2["Task 2: Thematic & Sustainable Instruments"]
    P2 --> T3["Task 3: Institutional & Policy Environment"]
    P3["Phase 3: Compare & Recommend"] --> T4["Task 4: Recommendations & Legal Roadmap"]
    T1 --> D1["Deliverable 1: Inception Note"]
    T1 --> D2["Deliverable 2: Legal & Regulatory Review Report"]
    T2 --> D2
    T3 --> D2
    T4 --> D3["Deliverable 3: Final Legal Assessment & Roadmap"]
```

